  "source": {
    "authoredBasis": "Deliberate false alternatives y=x and y=-x confuse proportional and reciprocal functions. Panels are centered at (-4,0) and (4,0); local axes have identical unit scale and a [-3,3] square window. Reciprocal curves use separate log-spaced segment branches and no x=0 point. Line candidates pass through the local origin. k=±1 represent shapes, not the same quantitative curve for every nonzero k.",
    "authoritativeText": [
      {
        "lesson": "alg7-c1-s3-n9",
        "exercise": "122",
        "text": "122. 作出函数 $y=\\frac{k}{x}$ 的草图（分 $k>0$ 和 $k<0$ 两种情况）。"
      }
    ],
